/raw.githubusercontent.com/njucckevin/OpenMobile-Code/faca68f386aff7277cdf494c84693c51090229c6/LICENSE"},{"method":"license_header","retrieved_at":"2026-10-19T06:54:58Z","role":"primary","sha256":"b09fcaf4fbc265223c2479c410beef2b98c5e687c78ecedf3452aa12ffc465f1","supports":["licenses.code"],"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/njucckevin/OpenMobile-Code/HEAD/LICENSE"}],"id":"github:njucckevin/openmobile-code","identifiers":{},"kind":"framework","last_verified_at":"2026-10-19T06:53:33Z","licenses":{"code":{"basis":"repository LICENSE header","declared":"Apache-2.0","retrieved_at":"2026-10-19T06:54:58Z","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/njucckevin/OpenMobile-Code/HEAD/LICENSE"},"data":null,"document":null,"weights":null},"links":[{"rel":"primary","url":"https://github.com/njucckevin/OpenMobile-Code"}],"name":"OpenMobile code","notes":"Official code of the OpenMobile paper (COLM 2026 per the README). AndroidWorld/ holds a modified AndroidWorld copy with exploration (random_walk_aw.py), rollout (run_diy.py), post-processing and evaluation scripts; task_synthesis/ builds screen context and environment memory and generates and judges instructions with a strong multimodal model; LlamaFactory/ registers the four released data splits and gives Qwen3-VL and Qwen3.5 SFT configs. The tree also contains an Android-Lab folder. The Qwen3VL agent in AndroidWorld/android_world/agents/seeact_v.py sends recent plain screenshots to an OpenAI-compatible endpoint and executes the returned mobile_use tool calls; UI-element metadata is saved for post-processing only. The policy-switching mode lets a strong model monitor a weaker actor and take over. The README's AndroidWorld success rates include Qwen3.5-9B results it identifies as unreproducible under vLLM.","published_at":null,"relations":[{"evidence_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/njucckevin/OpenMobile-Code/faca68f386aff7277cdf494c84693c51090229c6/README.md","target_id":"github:google-research/android_world","type":"uses"},{"evidence_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/njucckevin/OpenMobile-Code/faca68f386aff7277cdf494c84693c51090229c6/README.md","target_id":"arxiv:2604.15093","type":"documented_by"}],"review_status":"curated","scope":"core","summary":"OpenMobile pipeline for AndroidWorld: random-walk exploration, memory-based task-instruction synthesis, learner/expert policy-switching rollouts, conversion to LLaMA-Factory SFT data, and AndroidWorld evaluation.","topics":["data-generation","mobile-navigation","imitation-learning"],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://github.com/njucckevin/OpenMobile-Code"}
